[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n0_kit"
text = "# DRAFT
# Kit, Ralph the chandler's daughter, selling her last candles in the lane at dusk, night 0. Young, quick, curious about the new porter.
== start
(A girl with a tray of candles on a strap round her neck, her hood up against the rain.)
Kit: Candles! Last of the day, cheap as dirt. You're a brother. Are you the new one?
-> topics

== again
Kit: Two left, brother. Both for a ha'penny, and I'll throw in the tray.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n0_kit_porter] I'm the new porter. -> porter
* [if not n0_kit_candles] Who makes your candles? -> candles
* [if not n0_kit_abbey] Have you been inside? -> abbey

== porter [set n0_kit_porter]
Kit: I knew it! Everybody knew you were coming. Gib told Margery, and Margery told the lane.
Kit: You're younger than Brother Anselm. Well. Everybody's younger than Brother Anselm.
-> topics

== candles [set n0_kit_candles]
Kit: Father makes them and I sell them. Ralph the chandler. He's in the Keys, most like.
Kit: I'm at your gate most dusks with the tray. The brothers buy whatever I've got left.
Kit: Brother Ranulf would buy the tray and the strap, if I let him.
-> topics

== abbey [set n0_kit_abbey]
Kit: Past the gate? Never. Father says I'm not to, not ever.
Kit: Is it true there's a saint's finger in a glass box? And lights at night? You'll tell me, when you've seen.
-> topics

== leave
Kit: See you at the gate!
"
